# ── Data & outputs (code-only repository) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Everything here is either too large for GitHub or fully regenerable by
# re-running the notebooks against Google Earth Engine.

# Rasters -- CLMS IMD ~229 MB each, predicted maps 157-203 MB, GHSL 42-51 MB.
# All exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tif.aux.xml
*.ovr

# Trained models (RF ~21 MB) -- regenerable, and joblib is version-fragile
*.joblib
*.pkl
*.h5

# Sample points, metrics tables, figures
*.gpkg
*.gpkg-shm
*.gpkg-wal
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.qmd
*.csv
*.png
*.jpg
*.pdf

# ── Run outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every notebook writes under output/, laid out city / dataset / predictor:
#
#   output/milan/{clms,ghsl}/{embedding,median,stack,percentile}/
#   output/{hanoi,hcmc}/{embedding,median}/   per-city rasters and samples
#   output/transfer/{embedding,median}/       the two-city comparison files
#   output/milan/validation/                  photo-interpreted validation
#
# All of it is regenerable by re-running the notebooks against Earth Engine,
# and the predicted rasters exceed GitHub's 100 MB limit on their own.
output/

# ── Input data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# data/ holds only original inputs now: the CLMS and GHSL reference rasters,
# the Vietnam IMD rasters, the sample points and the photo-interpreted CSVs.
# None of it is ours to redistribute and none of it fits in the repository.
data/

# ── Report figures ARE version-controlled ────────────────────────────────────
# report/ is a self-contained Overleaf project: it must compile with no file
# outside it, so every figure the report cites has to be committed alongside
# report.tex. Two kinds live under report/figs/:
#
#   figs/*.png            built by code/make_report_figs.py from the fact base
#   figs/<run>/*.png      COPIES of notebook figures, refreshed by
#                         code/sync_figs.py, which mirrors each run directory
#                         under a name that says which run it is
#                         (milan_clms_percentile/, transfer_embedding/, ...)
#                         so the two runs that share
#                         fig01_transfer_comparison.png do not collide
#
# The copies duplicate gitignored originals on purpose. They are small (a few
# MB in total, each far below GitHub's limit) and they are what makes the
# shared folder complete; the originals stay ignored where the notebooks write
# them. Recursive globs, so the mirrored subdirectories are covered too.
!report/figs/
!report/figs/**/
!report/figs/**/*.png
!report/figs/*.png
# The GitHub QR code on the title page. Vector rather than raster, so the *.png
# negations above miss it, and without it the shared project is incomplete.
!report/figs/*.svg

# ── The fact base IS version-controlled ──────────────────────────────────────
# report/facts/ is the project's written record: the settled findings, the
# experiment map, the figure inventory, the figure gap list and the section
# plan. It moved out of data/ when data/ became inputs-only -- it is report
# prose, not data. Small, and the thing most worth having history for.
!report/facts/
!report/facts/*.md

docs/

# ── Secrets & credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Earth Engine / Google Cloud service-account keys must never be committed.
*.json
!requirements*.json
.env
.env.*
credentials/
*-service-account*
.config/earthengine/

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Jupyter ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
install_log.txt
*.log

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
report/*.docx

# ── The three deliverables ARE version-controlled ────────────────────────────
# report/ holds exactly three finished artefacts at its root, and they are what
# anyone outside the project is given:
#
#   report.tex        the source
#   report.pdf        the built report
#   IMD_Mapping.pptx  the presentation
#
# The PDF and the deck are builds rather than sources, which elsewhere in this
# file is reason to ignore something. They are tracked anyway: they are the
# deliverables, and a reader who cannot run XeLaTeX still needs them. Both
# override the blanket `*.pdf` and the presentation rule below.
!report/report.pdf
!report/IMD_Mapping.pptx

# Deck sources and drafts. Tens of MB of binary that diffs to nothing useful,
# and the same reasoning that excludes the rasters applies: these build the
# deck, they are not the deck. Everything that supports IMD_Mapping.pptx lives
# here -- the slide code, its figures, the builder notebooks -- and none of it
# is shared.
report/presentation/
# PowerPoint lock files, written while a deck is open and meaningless once it is
# closed. Anchored to the repo root would miss them; they sit beside the deck.
~$*
# LaTeX build artefacts. latexmkrc sends most of these to report/build/, but
# BibTeX writes .bbl and .blg beside report.tex regardless of $aux_dir, and
# both are regenerated from refs.bib on every build. Overleaf rebuilds them
# too, so they are not part of the shared project.
report/build/
report/*.bbl
report/*.blg
